ologic and laboratory surveillance data and the performance of the U.S. measles surveillance system\"}]}, {\"v\": \"before/after or trend\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"representing a more than seventeenfold increase over the mean number of cases reported during the first quarter of 2020–2023\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"A well-performing surveillance system was defined as one with ≥80% of cases meeting each of the following three criteria\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The potential for missed cases within two-case chains and outbreaks was assessed by measuring the interval between measles rash onset dates in each chain\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"unique sequences were defined as those differing by at least one nucleotide in the N-450 sequence\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"chains with more than one maximum incubation period (21 days) between cases could indicate a missing case in the chain\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}